course: dictionary
lesson: 6891
title: One word, two worlds: overthrow
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Overthrow can mean to remove someone from power by force. «In 1368 the Chinese Ming dynasty overthrew the Mongol Yuan dynasty.» The Ming forced the Yuan out of power, so overthrew means removed them by force.
explain: Overthrow can also be a noun: the overthrow of a ruler is that removal. In «Regime change means overthrowing, or forcing out, a foreign government», overthrowing is a verb with the same meaning. Watch the small word endings to see what job the word is doing.
explain: Context shows you which meaning you need. Kings, rulers, governments and armies point to power. A fielder, a ball and runs point to sport. Look at the words around the hard word before you guess.
explain: Check your meaning with a quick swap. Put "forced out of power" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning. You do not need to know every date to get the big idea.
fact: Overthrow is a verb and a noun: you can overthrow a ruler, or write about the overthrow of a ruler.
fact: The verb forms are overthrow, overthrows, overthrew, overthrowing and overthrown.
fact: «Overthrew» is the simple past tense of overthrow.
fact: In cricket and baseball, an overthrow is a throw that goes past the player meant to catch it, and it can give extra runs.
fact: «In 1789 the French Revolution overthrew the king's power.» Here overthrew means took power away from the king.
exercise: «In 1368 the Chinese Ming dynasty overthrew the Mongol Yuan dynasty.» What does overthrew mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Given a gift to | Thrown a ball too far | *Forced out of power
exercise: Ella says, «The fielder's overthrow let the batter run two extra runs.» What is an overthrow in this sentence? | *A throw that goes past the player meant to catch it | A loud shout | A ruler being removed from power | A kind of castle
exercise: Which word is the simple past tense of overthrow? | overthrowing | overthrows | overthrown | *overthrew
test: «The overthrow of the old king brought peace to the land.» In this sentence, what kind of word is overthrow? | *A noun, meaning the removal of a ruler | A verb, meaning to throw a ball | A name for a country | A kind of fruit
test: Which sentence uses overthrow in its cricket meaning? | The ruler was overthrown after a long war. | *A wild overthrow sent the ball past the keeper, and the batters ran extra runs. | The rebels planned to overthrow the government. | Magna Carta was signed in 1215.
exam: «The people hoped to overthrow the tyrant and bring back fair laws.» Which meaning fits best? | To count runs slowly | To paint a wall | To throw a ball past the catcher | *To remove by force from power
